# ---- Temporary debugging artefacts ----
#
# Scratch files written while debugging an integration by hand. They routinely
# hold whatever was needed to reproduce the problem: an access token, a session
# cookie, an account and its password.
#
# Ignored by pattern rather than by name because the next one will be called
# something else. A `.tmp-shopify-oauth.json` holding an account password and a
# live JWT sat untracked in the working tree, one `git add -A` away from a
# public repository.
#
# **These belong outside the project.** The ignore rule is the second line of
# defence, not the first — a file git cannot see is still a file sitting in a
# directory that gets zipped, synced, and screen-shared.
.tmp-*
*.tmp.json
*.local.json
oauth-debug*
*-token.json
*-credentials.json
